cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Kerr Black Hole: real-time general-relativistic ray tracing in the browser"
abstract: >-
  A real-time general-relativistic ray tracer for a rotating (Kerr) black hole
  that runs entirely in the browser on WebGL2. Light rays are integrated along
  null geodesics in Kerr-Schild coordinates, with a Novikov-Thorne accretion
  disk, Doppler beaming and gravitational redshift, a free-fall camera that
  crosses the event horizon, an EHT-style 1.3 mm view, video recording, and an
  English/Turkish interface. A TON 618 quasar mode derives the disk
  temperature from the mass, spin and Eddington ratio (Page-Thorne flux) and
  adds a hot corona, a disk wind, a jet and broad-line region clouds. The
  physics core is validated against analytic results.
